# Cleave

Live Milkdrop/libprojectM visualizer editor. The Windows standalone app is the product; CLI is for checkout, scripts, and CI.

- Entry: `python -m cleave play` (`cleave/viz/`). Commands: `separate`, `play`, `render`, `backup`, `restore`.
- Layers: up to eight, default four. Live at display rate; offline fps from `render.fps`.
- Data: `projects/<slug>/` (mix, `project.yaml`, `signals.json`, `stems/`). Override with `CLEAVE_DATA`.
- Config: parse and defaults in `cleave/config_schema/`. Repo-root `cleave-viz.yaml` is the project template.
- Stem PCM keeps native mono/stereo for projectM; mix playback is stereo; analysis for `signals.json` is mono.
- Work list: [docs/todos.md](docs/todos.md). Roadmap: [docs/roadmap.md](docs/roadmap.md). Usage: [README.md](README.md).
